{
 "_README": [
  "Depth below the body surface for every shipped structure of the Visible Human FEMALE (mm; shallowest point and median over the structure's surface), as computed by scripts/export_viewer_bundle.py (add_skin_depth) for the female bundle. Her body surface is the CT body silhouette (HU > -300) of BOTH CT blocks united on one grid (scripts/cryo/vhf_whole_body_skin.py), not a photograph. Derived data, regenerated 2026-09-12 after the lower-limb block, deltoid, rotator cuff, erector columns, upper-arm muscles and pectoralis minor were added; the legs->torso registration is +-4 mm in height, which bounds the depths below the knee to the same tolerance. Structures from the cryosection rules (ct_vhf_delt, ct_vhf_cuff, ct_vhf_armm, ct_vhf_pmr) carry the +-10 mm shoulder/arm registration uncertainty as well."
 ],
